{
  "id": "birthday-money",
  "title": "Compound interest ↔ your birthday money",
  "category": "Money",
  "width": 900,
  "height": 560,
  "background": "grid",
  "learning": {
    "goal": "See why money that earns interest on its interest grows slowly at first and then much faster, and why starting early matters more than the amount.",
    "question": "Your friend keeps their $200 in a drawer until age 25 and only then invests it at 7% a year. At 65, who has more, and by how much?",
    "answer": "You invested for 50 years: 200 × 1.07^50 ≈ $5,891. Your friend gets 40 years: 200 × 1.07^40 ≈ $2,995. Ten years of waiting cost about half the result, because the last decade is when the curve grows the most.",
    "caveat": "Real growth is not a smooth fixed rate: investments go up and down, and some years lose money. Broad stock index funds have historically averaged roughly 7% a year after inflation over long periods, but that is never guaranteed; a savings account pays less but is safer. Taxes and fees were left out."
  },
  "params": {
    "rate": {
      "label": "growth per year (%)",
      "min": 3,
      "max": 10,
      "step": 1,
      "value": 7
    }
  },
  "vars": {
    "r": "rate / 100",
    "i1": "200 * r",
    "i2": "200 * (1 + r) * r",
    "bx": 380,
    "by": 150,
    "bw": 470,
    "bh": 310,
    "final": "200 * (1 + r)^50",
    "simple": "200 * (1 + r * 50)",
    "ymax": "final * 1.25",
    "ex": "bx + bw",
    "ey": "by + bh - final / ymax * bh"
  },
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "at": [
        40,
        72
      ],
      "text": "$200 for your birthday. Spend it… or plant it?",
      "size": 40,
      "chapter": "The gift",
      "say": "You just turned 15 and got $200. What if that money could grow on its own?"
    },
    {
      "type": "prop",
      "name": "person",
      "at": [
        110,
        270
      ],
      "size": 110,
      "label": "you, 15",
      "id": "you"
    },
    {
      "type": "prop",
      "name": "coin",
      "at": [
        240,
        260
      ],
      "size": 60,
      "id": "gift"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "at": [
        240,
        180
      ],
      "text": "$200",
      "size": 32,
      "anchor": "middle",
      "style": {
        "color": "#2E8F62"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "at": [
        40,
        345
      ],
      "text": "year 1: +${i1:2}",
      "size": 28,
      "chapter": "Interest on interest",
      "say": "Put it somewhere that grows {rate}% a year. After one year you earn interest on your $200."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "at": [
        40,
        385
      ],
      "text": "year 2: +${i2:2}",
      "size": 28,
      "style": {
        "color": "#2F5BEA"
      },
      "say": "In year two you earn on the $200 and on last year's interest, so you get a bit more."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "at": [
        40,
        432
      ],
      "text": "that extra ${i2 - i1:2} is",
      "size": 24,
      "style": {
        "color": "#5E5A52"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "at": [
        40,
        462
      ],
      "text": "interest on your interest!",
      "size": 24,
      "style": {
        "color": "#5E5A52"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "polyline",
      "points": [
        [
          "bx",
          "by - 10"
        ],
        [
          "bx",
          "by + bh"
        ],
        [
          "bx + bw + 10",
          "by + bh"
        ]
      ],
      "style": {
        "width": 2.4
      },
      "chapter": "Fifty years later",
      "say": "That tiny extra repeats every year, and it keeps snowballing. Let's watch until you are 65."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "at": [
        "bx",
        "by + bh + 34"
      ],
      "text": "age 15",
      "size": 24,
      "style": {
        "color": "#5E5A52"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "at": [
        "bx + bw",
        "by + bh + 34"
      ],
      "text": "age 65",
      "size": 24,
      "anchor": "end",
      "style": {
        "color": "#5E5A52"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "plot",
      "fn": "200 * (1 + r * x)",
      "domain": [
        0,
        50
      ],
      "range": [
        0,
        "ymax"
      ],
      "box": {
        "x": "bx",
        "y": "by",
        "w": "bw",
        "h": "bh"
      },
      "style": {
        "color": "#8C8578",
        "width": 2.4,
        "dashed": true
      },
      "say": "If you only earned on the original $200, it would climb in a straight line."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "at": [
        "bx + 20",
        "by + 30"
      ],
      "text": "simple: ${simple:0}",
      "size": 26,
      "style": {
        "color": "#8C8578"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "pause",
      "ms": 400
    },
    {
      "type": "plot",
      "fn": "200 * (1 + r)^x",
      "domain": [
        0,
        50
      ],
      "range": [
        0,
        "ymax"
      ],
      "box": {
        "x": "bx",
        "y": "by",
        "w": "bw",
        "h": "bh"
      },
      "style": {
        "color": "#C8442C",
        "width": 3.4
      },
      "say": "With interest on interest, the curve is lazy for years, then bends upward hard."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "at": [
        "bx + 20",
        "by + 66"
      ],
      "text": "compound: ${final:0}",
      "size": 30,
      "style": {
        "color": "#C8442C"
      },
      "id": "compoundLabel"
    },
    {
      "type": "highlight",
      "from": [
        "bx + 18",
        "by + 72"
      ],
      "to": [
        "bx + 270",
        "by + 72"
      ],
      "thickness": 14,
      "chapter": "Time does the work",
      "say": "Same $200, never added a cent. Time did the work. Move the rate and watch."
    },
    {
      "type": "ellipse",
      "center": [
        "ex",
        "ey"
      ],
      "rx": 16,
      "ry": 16,
      "style": {
        "color": "#C8442C",
        "width": 2.4
      }
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en-US"
}